[probes]
?p1 What command is used to list model IDs available for a specific API key?
  = hcs models <provider>
  > README.md::"1. Compile a context file from your project" #ef515161ea43
?p2 How is the 'fidelity' field in a certificate calculated?
  = It is the mean points over probes, where correct is 1, partial is 0.5, and incorrect or abstained is 0.
  > SPEC.md::"7. Certificates" #3eff969f8f76
?p3 How does the system handle a symbol anchor when the symbol name is found but the content hash does not match?
  = It returns a status of 'stale' with a detail message indicating the symbol changed and the specific line range.
  > src/anchors.ts::checkSymbolAnchor #707de082a68e
?p4 What specific characters in a string cause looksLikePath to return false immediately?
  = Whitespace, asterisks, angle brackets, curly braces, dollar signs, and vertical bars.
  > src/audit.ts::looksLikePath #f26ac1eac79d
?p5 What exit code does the HCS CLI return for usage or syntax errors?
  = 2
  > src/cli.ts:59 #f5b114954bc5
?p6 What is the default maximum number of probes stored in a compiled HCS document?
  = 40
  > src/compile.ts:361 #d8eefb9c4046
?p7 What is the regular expression used to parse anchors, including paths, symbols, line ranges, and hashes?
  = /^(?:"([^"]+)"|([^\s"]+?))(?:::(?:"([^"]+)"|([^\s"#]+))|:(\d+)(?:-(\d+))?)?(?:\s+#([0-9a-f]{6,64}))?$/
  > src/format.ts::ANCHOR_RE #53922ef67757
?p8 What string constant is used to tag claims that contain high-severity injection patterns?
  = suspect
  > src/guard.ts::SUSPECT_TAG #bd0e626c3173
?p9 What happens if an anchor path resolves to a location outside the project root?
  = The SourceCache returns null for the lines, treating it as a hostile anchor or non-existent file.
  > src/anchors.ts::SourceCache #933859786314
?p10 How does the auditor handle line number suffixes (e.g., ':10-20') at the end of a path candidate?
  = It removes them using a regular expression before checking if the path exists.
  > src/audit.ts::findPathReferences #062b34fc2880
?p11 How does the CLI handle multiple judge models during the scoring process?
  = Agreement is reported, and the stricter verdict counts.
  > src/cli.ts:49 #c6fef185ef4a
?p12 How does the compiler handle claims that contain text identified as high risk?
  = It adds a SUSPECT_TAG to the claim for human review and does not render it by default.
  > src/compile.ts::extractChunk #b8d51ae71481
?p13 How are multiple lines of a probe answer handled during parsing?
  = They are joined with a single space.
  > src/format.ts:158 #f2d6aebaf686
?p14 Which severity level is assigned to patterns that mention running shell commands like 'curl' or 'rm -rf'?
  = low
  > src/guard.ts::PATTERNS #467c0d579d52
?p15 What is the specific length of the hash used for anchors?
  = 12 characters.
  > src/anchors.ts::HASH_LENGTH #0330f2780307
?p16 Why is a missing 'bare' file reference treated differently than a missing path with directories?
  = A bare file name might be a generic mention rather than a specific file reference, so it only triggers a warning.
  > src/audit.ts::PathReference #84a49e01386c
?p17 What happens to existing certificates when an HCS file is re-hashed during a seal operation?
  = They are cleared because the sources changed and earlier scores no longer apply.
  > src/cli.ts:279 #906e967e049c
?p18 What happens to existing certificates in a document when it is recompiled?
  = They are cleared because the content has changed and old scores no longer apply.
  > src/compile.ts:370 #809d27283f65
?p19 What specific header keys have a predefined order during serialization?
  = title, root, created, updated, generator, source-files, and source-tokens.
  > src/format.ts::serialize #ae589dcd81a8
?p20 How does the scanSource function handle line numbering?
  = It uses 1-based indexing by adding 1 to the loop index.
  > src/guard.ts::scanSource #4653fed397c1
?p21 What is the default reasoning budget constant REASONING_BUDGET set to?
  = 4096
  > src/llm.ts::REASONING_BUDGET #c657d5bd2296
?p22 What server version is exported by src/mcp.ts?
  = 0.2.0
  > src/mcp.ts::SERVER_VERSION #230a12297af3
?p23 What is the default importance value for a hand-written claim if no iN tag is present?
  = 5
  > src/render.ts::importance #de4a375ca726
?p24 What is the default number of resamples used in bootstrapCI?
  = 2000
  > src/score.ts::bootstrapCI #09a88d67acf9
?p25 What error message is thrown by parseConversation when the conversation format is unrecognized?
  = unrecognized conversation format (expected an array of messages or {messages: [...]})
  > src/snapshot.ts::parseConversation #44e353c78333
?p26 What is the default maximum byte size for collected source files?
  = 262144
  > src/sources.ts::collectSources #c0440aacf4c2
?p27 What extensions are recognized as Python by languageOf?
  = py, pyi
  > src/symbols.ts::languageOf #b03b3b4eb531
?p28 What is the maximum retry wait time constant MAX_RETRY_WAIT_MS set to in milliseconds?
  = 120000
  > src/llm.ts::MAX_RETRY_WAIT_MS #ffea888e2d7e
?p29 What is the default max_lines per anchor in hcs_expand if not specified or invalid?
  = 120
  > src/mcp.ts:155 #5c8200f6a7d8
?p30 What fallback title is used in renderContext if doc.headers.title is undefined?
  = Untitled
  > src/render.ts::renderContext #31ee6bf0bfa6
?p31 What maximum number of judges are supported by judgesOf?
  = two
  > src/score.ts::judgesOf #d01411649f69
?p32 What role is explicitly filtered out and excluded from the parsed messages?
  = system
  > src/snapshot.ts::parseConversation #44e353c78333
?p33 What file extension regex is used to identify documentation files?
  = /\.(md|mdx|markdown|txt|rst|adoc|org|tex|html?)$/i
  > src/sources.ts::DOC_EXT #a4d7ec12b0bc
?p34 What is the default maxLines parameter in enclosingSymbol?
  = 80
  > src/symbols.ts::enclosingSymbol #c9e2964b3c56
?p35 Which header does authHint check to see if an egress proxy reported its own view of an authentication failure?
  = x-proxy-error
  > src/llm.ts::authHint #ffdcc6547ae0
?p36 What HTML comment header is added at the beginning of transcripts generated by toTranscript?
  = <!-- hcs:transcript -->
  > src/snapshot.ts::toTranscript #c919125008f9
?p37 What string prefix identifies a conversation profile in profileFor?
  = <!-- hcs:transcript -->
